174, "no_speech_prob": 0.03952030465006828}, {"id": 39, "seek": 15540, "start": 174.4, "end": 176.4, "text": " The loop will start from j is equal to 0.", "tokens": [51314, 440, 6367, 486, 722, 490, 361, 307, 2681, 281, 1958, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29048873237941575, "compression_ratio": 1.8623853211009174, "no_speech_prob": 0.03952030465006828}, {"id": 40, "seek": 15540, "start": 176.4, "end": 179.4, "text": " Where will the loop go until the value of j is less than the ending index.", "tokens": [51414, 2305, 486, 264, 6367, 352, 1826, 264, 2158, 295, 361, 307, 1570, 813, 264, 8121, 8186, 13, 51564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29048873237941575, "compression_ratio": 1.8623853211009174, "no_speech_prob": 0.03952030465006828}, {"id": 41, "seek": 15540, "start": 179.4, "end": 183.4, "text": " That means, it is less than the pivot until the value of j is plus plus.", "tokens": [51564, 663, 1355, 11, 309, 307, 1570, 813, 264, 14538, 1826, 264, 2158, 295, 361, 307, 1804, 1804, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29048873237941575, "compression_ratio": 1.8623853211009174, "no_speech_prob": 0.03952030465006828}, {"id": 42, "seek": 18340, "start": 183.4, "end": 191.4, "text": " I will compare every time that my element, that is, j is less than equal to my pivot.", "tokens": [50364, 286, 486, 6794, 633, 565, 300, 452, 4478, 11, 300, 307, 11, 361, 307, 1570, 813, 2681, 281, 452, 14538, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27615467823334855, "compression_ratio": 2.1009174311926606, "no_speech_prob": 0.015482691116631031}, {"id": 43, "seek": 18340, "start": 191.4, "end": 194.4, "text": " If it is less than equal to, then I have to make a place in that case.", "tokens": [50764, 759, 309, 307, 1570, 813, 2681, 281, 11, 550, 286, 362, 281, 652, 257, 1081, 294, 300, 1389, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27615467823334855, "compression_ratio": 2.1009174311926606, "no_speech_prob": 0.015482691116631031}, {"id": 44, "seek": 18340, "start": 194.4, "end": 198.4, "text": " And how do we make a place? First we do the i plus plus, then we do the swap.", "tokens": [50914, 400, 577, 360, 321, 652, 257, 1081, 30, 2386, 321, 360, 264, 741, 1804, 1804, 11, 550, 321, 360, 264, 18135, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27615467823334855, "compression_ratio": 2.1009174311926606, "no_speech_prob": 0.015482691116631031}, {"id": 45, "seek": 18340, "start": 198.4, "end": 200.4, "text": " So, how will we do the swap? We will take the temporary variable.", "tokens": [51114, 407, 11, 577, 486, 321, 360, 264, 18135, 30, 492, 486, 747, 264, 13413, 7006, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27615467823334855, "compression_ratio": 2.1009174311926606, "no_speech_prob": 0.015482691116631031}, {"id": 46, "seek": 18340, "start": 200.4, "end": 203.4, "text": " I will store the value of j in the array of j.", "tokens": [51214, 286, 486, 3531, 264, 2158, 295, 361, 294, 264, 10225, 295, 361, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27615467823334855, "compression_ratio": 2.1009174311926606, "no_speech_prob": 0.015482691116631031}, {"id": 47, "seek": 18340, "start": 203.4, "end": 208.4, "text": " Then I will store the value of i in the array of j.", "tokens": [51364, 1396, 286, 486, 3531, 264, 2158, 295, 741, 294, 264, 10225, 295, 361, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27615467823334855, "compression_ratio": 2.1009174311926606, "no_speech_prob": 0.015482691116631031}, {"id": 48, "seek": 18340, "start": 208.4, "end": 212.4, "text": " After that, I will store the value of j in the array of i.", "tokens": [51614, 2381, 300, 11, 286, 486, 3531, 264, 2158, 295, 361, 294, 264, 10225, 295, 741, 13, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27615467823334855, "compression_ratio": 2.1009174311926606, "no_speech_prob": 0.015482691116631031}, {"id": 49, "seek": 21240, "start": 212.4, "end": 216.4, "text": " So, I have compared every time that the value of the current element is less than the pivot.", "tokens": [50364, 407, 11, 286, 362, 5347, 633, 565, 300, 264, 2158, 295, 264, 2190, 4478, 307, 1570, 813, 264, 14538, 13, 50564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26844820530294516, "compression_ratio": 2.036290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 0.008860614150762558}, {"id": 50, "seek": 21240, "start": 216.4, "end": 218.4, "text": " If it is less, then I will have to make a place.", "tokens": [50564, 759, 309, 307, 1570, 11, 550, 286, 486, 362, 281, 652, 257, 1081, 13, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26844820530294516, "compression_ratio": 2.036290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 0.008860614150762558}, {"id": 51, "seek": 21240, "start": 218.4, "end": 221.4, "text": " To make a place, there will be i plus plus and after that, we will swap.", "tokens": [50664, 1407, 652, 257, 1081, 11, 456, 486, 312, 741, 1804, 1804, 293, 934, 300, 11, 321, 486, 18135, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26844820530294516, "compression_ratio": 2.036290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 0.008860614150762558}, {"id": 52, "seek": 21240, "start": 221.4, "end": 226.4, "text": " That means, the value on the index i and the value on the index j will be swapped.", "tokens": [50814, 663, 1355, 11, 264, 2158, 322, 264, 8186, 741, 293, 264, 2158, 322, 264, 8186, 361, 486, 312, 50011, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26844820530294516, "compression_ratio": 2.036290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 0.008860614150762558}, {"id": 53, "seek": 21240, "start": 226.4, "end": 230.4, "text": " In this way, I have analyzed all the elements that are smaller than my pivot.", "tokens": [51064, 682, 341, 636, 11, 286, 362, 28181, 439, 264, 4959, 300, 366, 4356, 813, 452, 14538, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26844820530294516, "compression_ratio": 2.036290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 0.008860614150762558}, {"id": 54, "seek": 21240, "start": 230.4, "end": 232.4, "text": " Now, let's put the pivot at the right place.", "tokens": [51264, 823, 11, 718, 311, 829, 264, 14538, 412, 264, 558, 1081, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26844820530294516, "compression_ratio": 2.036290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 0.008860614150762558}, {"id": 55, "seek": 21240, "start": 232.4, "end": 236.4, "text": " To put the pivot at the right place, I will have to do this work only one last time.", "tokens": [51364, 1407, 829, 264, 14538, 412, 264, 558, 1081, 11, 286, 486, 362, 281, 360, 341, 589, 787, 472, 1036, 565, 13, 51564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26844820530294516, "compression_ratio": 2.036290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 0.008860614150762558}, {"id": 56, "seek": 23640, "start": 236.4, "end": 239.4, "text": " That means, I will do the same work here.", "tokens": [50364, 663, 1355, 11, 286, 486, 360, 264, 912, 589, 510, 13, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27057129996163504, "compression_ratio": 2.1095238095238096, "no_speech_prob": 0.1506970226764679}, {"id": 57, "seek": 23640, "start": 239.4, "end": 244.4, "text": " i plus plus, then my swap logic.", "tokens": [50514, 741, 1804, 1804, 11, 550, 452, 18135, 9952, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27057129996163504, "compression_ratio": 2.1095238095238096, "no_speech_prob": 0.1506970226764679}, {"id": 58, "seek": 23640, "start": 244.4, "end": 246.4, "text": " What will I store in the temporary here?", "tokens": [50764, 708, 486, 286, 3531, 294, 264, 13413, 510, 30, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27057129996163504, "compression_ratio": 2.1095238095238096, "no_speech_prob": 0.1506970226764679}, {"id": 59, "seek": 23640, "start": 246.4, "end": 249.4, "text": " I will store the value of the pivot in the temporary here.", "tokens": [50864, 286, 486, 3531, 264, 2158, 295, 264, 14538, 294, 264, 13413, 510, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27057129996163504, "compression_ratio": 2.1095238095238096, "no_speech_prob": 0.1506970226764679}, {"id": 60, "seek": 23640, 